DECISIONS & REASONING
---------------------

Decision 1: Use shadcn/ui Card component
  - Context: Need consistent card styling across dashboard
  - Rationale: Project already uses shadcn/ui, maintains consistency
  - Evidence: Existing components (IntensitySlider) follow this pattern
  - Trade-offs: Locked into shadcn/ui API
  - Impact: Easy to maintain, accessible by default

Decision 2: Co-locate Storybook stories with components
  - Context: Project structure needs clarification
  - Rationale: Storybook best practice for discoverability
  - Evidence: Existing stories (IntensitySlider.stories.tsx) are co-located
  - Trade-offs: None, this is the standard pattern
  - Impact: Easier to find and maintain stories

Decision 3: Make components presentational (props-based)
  - Context: Components need to be reusable and testable
  - Rationale: Clean Architecture - components are presentation layer
  - Evidence: Components should not directly access stores
  - Trade-offs: Parent component must pass props (but this is correct)
  - Impact: More testable, reusable in different contexts

Decision 4: Use lucide-react for icons
  - Context: Need icons for Brain, Lightbulb, ClipboardCheck, Flame
  - Rationale: Project already uses lucide-react (confirmed in package.json)
  - Evidence: Existing usage in project
  - Trade-offs: None, icons are tree-shaken
  - Impact: Consistent icon style

Decision 5: Implement milestone-based styling for StreakDisplay
  - Context: Need to celebrate user achievements
  - Rationale: Gamification increases engagement and motivation
  - Evidence: Research shows positive reinforcement improves habit formation
  - Trade-offs: More complex CSS logic
  - Impact: Better UX, encourages consistent tracking
  - Confidence: High - this is a proven pattern

Decision 6: Add tap-to-refresh for QuickInsightCard
  - Context: User may want to see different insights
  - Rationale: Gives control to user, increases engagement
  - Evidence: Similar pattern in mobile apps (pull-to-refresh)
  - Trade-offs: Optional feature, doesn't complicate core functionality
  - Impact: Enhanced interactivity, optional usage

